   <property name="text">
    <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rum is a distilled spirit crafted from sugarcane byproducts like molasses or directly from sugarcane juice. Unlike grain-based spirits such as whiskey or beer, rum draws its richness from the tropical world of sugar plantations and carries a complex flavor profile shaped by various production processes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Barbados proudly claims to be the birthplace of rum. The earliest mention of the word &amp;quot;rum&amp;quot; dates to a lease agreement written on March 30, 1650, at Three Houses plantation in St. Philip, Barbados. Mount Gay Distillery, established in 1703, is recognized as the world's oldest commercial rum distillery.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The traditional rum-making process includes gathering molasses, fermentation, distillation, maturation, and optionally blending and coloring or sweetening. Today, rum remains a symbol of Caribbean culture and creativity. From the smoky, aged rums of Jamaica to the light, crisp rums of Puerto Rico and the agricole varieties of Martinique, rum spans a wide flavor spectrum. It's sipped neat, mixed into classic cocktails, and celebrated worldwide for its deep cultural and historical significance. Now, it's your turn to brew a batch—let's dive in!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
   </property>
